{
  "description" : "The admin users section (admin contract section 12): GET /api/admin/users[/{id}], GET /api/admin/invitations, POST /api/admin/users, POST /api/admin/invitations/{id}/resend, DELETE /api/admin/invitations/{id}. Setup: application 'orders' (flowcatalyst.application); the platform answers the routes in 'platform' ('METHOD path' to {status, body}) unless a case has 'override' entries of the same shape. The service account is the caller on the platform; the signed-in user's permissions decide first (users:view, :invite, :resend, :revoke; a wildcard grant counts): without the operation's permission the answer is 403 FORBIDDEN and the platform is not called. 'calls' lists the platform requests in order as 'METHOD path' (the application code in a path is always 'orders'); 'platformBody' is the JSON the first call sent. Lists page by cursor = the next platform page number (nextCursor present when (page + 1) * limit < total); roles shown are the application's own ('orders:'-prefixed); a role filter keeps only own roles and asks nothing when none is left; an id outside [A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,64} is 404 without a call; invite refuses another application's role (403 ROLE_APP_FORBIDDEN) before the platform. The invite link is a credential: 'answerHasLink' is true only when the caller asked for it (returnInviteLink), whatever the platform sends, and no list carries it. A platform answer of 400/409/422, or 403/500 with a reason of its own, is passed on in the platform's words (status, code, message; 500 becomes 502; a 403 FORBIDDEN 'client is not available to this application' becomes CLIENT_NOT_AVAILABLE); any other failure is 502 PLATFORM_ERROR with a message that names no host, token or platform text; a platform 404 of a single record is 404 USER_NOT_FOUND / INVITATION_NOT_FOUND.",
